 899:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   * @brief  Enable ExtiLine Rising Edge Trigger for Lines in range 0 to 31
 900:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   * @note The configurable wakeup lines are edge-triggered. No glitch must be
 901:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       generated on these lines. If a rising edge on a configurable interrupt
 902:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       line occurs during a write operation in the EXTI_RTSR register, the
 903:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       pending bit is not set.
 904:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       Rising and falling edge triggers can be set for
 905:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       the same interrupt line. In this case, both generate a trigger
 906:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   *       condition.
 907:.sdk/SR5E1_MCTK-1.3.0/include/LL_Library/sr5e1_ll_exti.h ****   * @rmtoll RTSR1        RTx           LL_EXTI_EnableRisingTrig_0_31
